<title>JAPAN: Mikuni assigns preliminary bond credit ratings.</title>
<headline>Mikuni assigns preliminary bond credit ratings.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mikuni and Co Ltd said on Friday it had assigned the following preliminary ratings to planned bond issues:</p>
<p>-AAA-</p>
<p>Toyota Motor Corp, $1 billion unsecured due 2002.</p>
<p>Nippon Resibon Corp, 13 million Swiss Francs unsecured due 2001, private placement, guaranteed by Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi.  </p>
<p>-BBB-</p>
<p>Yokogawa Electric Corp, 10 billion yen unsecured due 2002.</p>
<p>-BB-</p>
<p>Acom Co Ltd, 10 billion yen unsecured due 2001.</p>
<p>Hiroshima Gas Co Ltd, three billion yen unsecured due 2004.</p>
<p>Nissan Motor Co Ltd,</p>
<p>20 billion yen unsecured due 2002.</p>
<p>20 billion yen unsecured due 2004.</p>
</text>
